    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 3/3 tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional `postcode` validation for owners. When present, a postcode must be 4 digits and, if the owner's city maps to a known region, fall within that region's range; a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. It's stored and returned, and absence keeps the request backward-compatible.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` field (4-digit string) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so both the request (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response (`OwnerDto`, via `allOf`) DTOs carry it (regenerated at build).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `postcode` column. Also fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner inserts (which broke with the new column) by appending a `NULL`.\n\n4. **`CityRegion.java`** \u2014 Added the region\u2192postcode-range table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) and a `postcodeRangeOf(city)` helper returning `null` for cities with no known region.\n\n5. **`ValidateOwner.java`** \u2014 Added optional-when-present postcode validation (4-digit format + region range), mirroring the existing email handling, throwing a new checked `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n6. **`InvalidPostcodeException` + handler + escalation YAML** \u2014 New checked exception mapped to a 400 response, following the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` pattern.\n\n7. **`ApplyOwner.java`** \u2014 Copies `postcode` on the PUT path so updates persist it too.\n\nThe three checkpoints \u2014 valid postcode stored/returned, owner without postcode accepted, malformed postcode rejected with 400 \u2014 all pass.",
